  "details": "While the current muting functionality is fine when you want to mute certain people, it can become cumbersome when you want to mute everyone EXCEPT specific people, as the only option is to mute everyone else. Earmuff mode is useful in this regard to an extent, but it still struggles if you want to hear a specific person from a distance, or if there are many other people within the range.\n\nI propose adding a \"Focus mode\", which would function similarly to the solo option in most audio programs. Focus mode can be toggled on and off in the same manner as earmuff mode. When enabled, all voice audio will be muted. Individual users can then be focused (in the same menu as you would mute) to selectively listen to them. This can be denoted with a yellow speaker/sound icon above focused users to distinguish it from muting. Multiple people can be focused at one time.",
